      <h2>PASTURE AND POULTRY FEED</h2>
      <img class="text-decoration-right" src="/assets/img/Smoky Mountain Acres/text-decoration-half-leaf.webp" alt="">
    </div>
    <p>Pasture gives the flock room to behave like chickens, while balanced feed supports their nutritional needs.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="container"><div class="row gy-4 align-items-center"><div class="col-lg-5"><img src="/assets/img/Smoky Mountain Acres/BabyChicks1.webp" class="img-fluid" alt="Young chicks at Smoky Mountain Acres"></div><div class="col-lg-7 content"><h3>Organic Supplemental Feed</h3><p>We supplement what the chickens find outdoors with organic poultry feed formulated for the needs of laying hens. Pasture and organic feed are complementary; access to pasture does not mean a laying flock can meet every nutritional requirement from forage alone.</p><p>When we say our chickens receive organic feed, we are describing the feed we choose. We are not claiming USDA Organic certification for eggs or farm products unless the applicable certification is in place.</p></div></div></div>
</section>

<section id="egg-availability" class="about section paper-texture">
  <div class="container" data-aos="fade-up"><div class="row gy-4 align-items-center"><div class="col-lg-5 order-lg-2"><img src="/assets/img/Smoky Mountain Acres/BarredRock2.webp" class="img-fluid" alt="Barred Rock chicken in the farm flock"></div><div class="col-lg-7 order-lg-1 content"><h2>Eggs and Occasional Chickens</h2><p>Egg availability changes with daylight, weather, flock size, age, molting, and season. We share eggs when the hens are actually producing a surplus rather than promising year-round inventory.</p><p>We sometimes have chickens available as well, but availability, breed, age, and purpose vary. Check the livestock page for current status and request updates for sold-out items.</p><a href="/livestock/" class="cta-btn">View Chicken and Egg Availability</a></div></div></div>
</section>

